## Why Reproducibility Is A Product Feature

The exemplar connects a locked environment, committed configuration, checksum-identified input, importable Hamilton/Polars analysis, deterministic output, and regression test. Documentation can therefore point to executable evidence instead of describing an unverified workflow.

Networked acquisition is intentionally separate from reproduction. A synchronized environment should reproduce the exemplar without network access.

## Why These Tools

- `uv` owns project dependencies, locking, and commands.
- Pydantic validates configuration and result boundaries.
- Polars provides explicit lazy tabular transformations.
- Hamilton makes the dataflow graph inspectable.

Heavier preferred tools remain thresholded rather than preinstalled.
